    "created_at": "2016-06-09T19:34:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T19:34:29Z",
    "body": "> Is that something that is easy to implement?\n\nIt's easy in Gecko.  That said, what should happen with:\n\n```\nwindow.customElements.define(\"valid-name\", Set);\n```\n\n?  Detecting ES built-in constructors might be a bit more annoying...  I guess it can just be allowed and throw due to the failing brand checks.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
