    "created_at": "2016-06-09T19:38:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T19:38:51Z",
    "body": "Maybe we should just prohibit HTMLElement and interfaces inheriting from it, as those are the only ones that would actually pass the brand check later and thus be actually problematic. The others (including both ES things like `Set` and platform things like `Worker`) are in some sense no different from trying to register `class C { }` or `class D extends HTMLElement { constructor() { /* no super() */ } }`.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/225003579/reactions",
