    "created_at": "2016-06-09T20:11:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T20:11:48Z",
    "body": "Because all those cases will fail to create an element, whereas if you pass something like `HTMLButtonElement`, it will actually work---sort of. (It would create an instance of `HTMLButtonElement` whose local name was `a-valid-custom-element-name`, which seems pretty bad.)\n",
